For Sonar cube scanner if you have jenkins please use plugins - SonarQube Scanner for Jenkins
-----------------------------------------------------------------

1. Download and Extract SonarScannerRun the following commands to download the package via wget, extract it using unzip, and move it to the /opt/ system directory:bash# Update package list and install unzip if you haven't already
sudo apt update && sudo apt install unzip wget -y

# Download the SonarScanner CLI binary package - wget https://binaries.sonarsource.com/Distribution/sonar-scanner-cli/sonar-scanner-cli-5.0.1.3006-linux.zip

# Unzip the package - unzip sonar-scanner-cli-5.0.1.3006-linux.zip

# Move the extracted directory to /opt for system-wide availability - sudo mv sonar-scanner-5.0.1.3006-linux /opt/sonar-scanner

Use code with caution.(Note: You can check the SonarSource Binaries Repository if you need to grab a different specific version).2. Configure Environment VariablesTo make the sonar-scanner command executable from any path or directory in your terminal, add it to your profile system configuration:bash# Append the binary path to your .bashrc file
echo 'export PATH="$PATH:/opt/sonar-scanner/bin"' >> ~/.bashrc

# Reload your terminal profile to apply changes immediately
source ~/.bashrc
Use code with caution.
3. Verify the InstallationOpen a new shell session or use the refreshed one to confirm that the package is correctly recognized: sonar-scanner -v 
